    "result_text": "There's only one test in the suite, and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners`, then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. I made two minimal, well-placed changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` field to the `Owner` response schema (readOnly, not part of the editable `OwnerFields`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` on the existing `toOwnerDto(Owner)` method computing `displayName` as `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored names.\n\nThe logic lives where it belongs: the DTO shape in the OpenAPI contract, the name-to-DTO derivation in the MapStruct mapper that already owns Owner\u2192OwnerDto conversion. No responder or function class needed changing, since every owner response already flows through `toOwnerDto`. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
